.TH SETRESUID 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
setresuid \- sets real, effective and saved user ids; (uid_t)-1 leaves an id unchanged
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.B int setresuid(uid_t real, uid_t effective, uid_t saved);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sets real, effective and saved user IDs; (uid_t)-1 leaves an ID unchanged. This is a direct per-thread syscall.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the syscall result on success, or \-1 with errno set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR setresuid (2)
